Runtime dependency (NOT part of this package's source)
------------------------------------------------------

  cua-driver — https://github.com/trycua/cua (MIT)

  All desktop input simulation and screen observation is performed by
  cua-driver; this plugin does not implement input simulation itself. The
  plugin spawns the cua-driver binary, and when the binary is missing while
  auto-install is enabled it may bootstrap it once (official installer, or a
  GitHub Release download verified by SHA256). See the `dsh.permissions`
  block in package.json for the exact commands, write paths and failure
  boundaries.

Upstream code changes are pulled with `git subtree pull` (see the repository
contributor notes). This fork's README and documentation are maintained
locally and are deliberately NOT synced from upstream.
